/*
  SuspenseProgressBoundary.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0141 · SuspenseProgressBoundary (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web boundary itself
  (components/feedback/SuspenseProgressBoundary.tsx) renders NO translatable copy — it is anonymous, it
  only swaps `children` for a `fallback` and calls no `t()`. The one locale-sensitive string belongs to
  the bar the boundary drives: the web `components/feedback/TopProgress.tsx` reads
  `t('global.loading', 'Loading')` for the progress bar's `aria-label`. That key is mirrored verbatim
  below so the native bar's VoiceOver label resolves through the same P1/S10 contract, and the Swift
  sources hold no English literals.

  The remaining entry is the native accessibility addition for the fallback branch — the spoken identity
  of the loading region while the fallback is mounted (the "never a silent box" peer of the web fallback
  subtree). These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time;
  they are kept in a per-surface table ("SuspenseProgressBoundary") so each parallel surface prompt owns
  its own strings. In test / preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value below, keeping the
  labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Web key mirrored from `TopProgress` (the bar this boundary drives) --- */

